willing to work with Germany short-term against France, but I will take Denmark/Sweden later if the opportunity arises. I should be warm and cooperative but avoid binding commitments. I need to confirm my NTH move (which benefits Germany by blocking France) and suggest future coordination. I won't mention Sweden - that's a potential future target I don't want to reveal.", "to": "GERMANY", "message": "Excellent, Germany. Your move to Denmark is well-timed — it secures that critical space before France can reach it. This spring, my fleet at Edinburgh will move to the North Sea, positioning for Norway in the fall. Having you hold Denmark blocks any French attempt to slip north through that corridor, which protects both our interests.

I propose we stay in close communication as the game develops. If France makes aggressive moves toward either of us, we can coordinate a response. My fleets will keep the northern seas clear, and your position on the continent can check French land expansion.

What are your thoughts on Sweden? And do you see any threat from France's current position that we should monitor?", "proposal": "non_aggression_and_coordination", "commitment": "F EDI -> NTH"}
